<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Orange Cake Formula</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main class="page">
    <section class="panel wide">
      <div class="statusbar">
        <span class="dot"></span>
        <span>OPP INTERNAL SYSTEM</span>
        <span class="status-right">REACTOR FORMULA NODE</span>
      </div>

      <h1>Orange Cake Formula</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Internal calculator for citrus enrichment batches used by the Orange Power Plant reactor team.
      </p>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Target batch</h2>
          <p>
            The reactor requires orange cake enriched to <strong>8%</strong>. Operators use this console
            to validate dummy ingredient ratios before a batch is sent to backup validation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Operator note</h2>
          <p>
            Formula strings are normalized by the application before they are processed by the backend.
            Some test values may behave differently than plain text.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sample">
        <span>Example operator input</span>
        <code>5 * orangejuice + 5 * orangium</code>
      </div>

      <p class="small">
        OPP-REDIS-CALC-01 · Internal Redis Formula Console · Backup validation route enabled
      </p>

      <a class="button" href="/calculator">Open calculator</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
